# generator outcome per malformed/edge input
# Every row runs in a fresh child process, so a non-unwinding crash is classified as `ABORTED (signal n)`
# instead of killing this catalog. A NEW panic is a regression: malformed input must error gracefully. A
# committed PANIC entry is a tracked-known rejection (see the fixture's comments); flipping it to `error
# (graceful)` is a fix. The parent requires a child sentinel before accepting any ordinary exit status.

alias_plain_group_array_element error (graceful)
